{"prdMarkdown":"# Product Requirements Document (PRD): Dashboard Dark Mode\n\n## Problem Statement\nOperators using the internal ops dashboard (`README.md`) frequently work across varied lighting environments and extended shifts. The application currently lacks theme customization, leading to eye strain and reduced readability in low-light environments.\n\n## Goals\n- Provide an accessible and intuitive theme toggle control in the dashboard navigation header (`src/components/Header.jsx`).\n- Persist user theme selection across sessions using browser storage (`localStorage`) so that preferences are retained between visits without requiring a page re-configuration.\n- Ensure smooth, predictable transitions between light and dark modes across all views rendered under `src/App.jsx`.\n\n## Non-Goals\n- Synchronizing theme preferences to remote user profiles or making backend API changes via `src/api/client.js`.\n- Supporting custom themes, high-contrast themes, or custom color palettes beyond standard light and dark options.\n- Automatic scheduled theme transitions (e.g., switching based on time of day).\n\n## User Impact\n- **Ops Engineers / Dashboard Users**: Improved visual ergonomics during night shifts or low-light monitoring, leading to reduced visual fatigue.\n- **Consistency**: Users will not need to re-select their theme on every session or page refresh.\n\n## Open Product Questions\n1. **Default Theme Resolution**: When a user visits the dashboard for the first time with no saved preference in `localStorage`, should the system automatically inherit the operating system preference (via `prefers-color-scheme`), or should it default to light mode?\n2. **Toggle Presentation**: What visual control is preferred in `src/components/Header.jsx` (e.g., an icon toggle with sun/moon glyphs, a standard toggle switch, or a labeled text button)?","trdMarkdown":"# Technical Requirements Document (TRD): Dashboard Dark Mode\n\n## Architecture Notes\n- **Theme State Management**: Introduce a React Theme Context / Provider at the root level in `src/App.jsx`. This provider will manage the current theme state (`'light'` | `'dark'`), handle state transitions, and apply the appropriate class or attribute (e.g., `data-theme=\"dark\"`) to `document.documentElement`.\n- **Header Control**: Integrate the toggle component into `src/components/Header.jsx`. The toggle will consume the Theme Context and expose accessible controls with appropriate ARIA attributes (e.g., `aria-pressed`, `aria-label=\"Toggle dark mode\"`).\n- **Token & Styling Strategy**: `package.json` currently lacks a CSS framework or CSS-in-JS library. Styling should be implemented via CSS custom properties (variables) defined at the root level and toggled via a `data-theme` attribute on the root DOM node, allowing theme variables to cascade down the component tree.\n- **Storage Persistence**: Theme preference will be stored directly in `localStorage` under a dedicated key (e.g., `dashboard_theme`). No updates to `src/api/client.js` are required.\n\n## Edge Cases & Dependencies\n- **Styling Architecture (`package.json`)**: With no utility library (e.g., Tailwind) or CSS library in `package.json`, styling tokens (backgrounds, text, borders) must be declared cleanly in CSS without breaking existing component styling.\n- **Icon Assets (`package.json`)**: No icon library (such as `lucide-react` or `react-icons`) exists in dependencies. The toggle UI in `src/components/Header.jsx` must either use inline SVG icons or add a lightweight dependency.\n- **Flash of Incorrect Theme (FOUC)**: Initializing theme state inside `useEffect` or React component mount can cause a visual flicker from light to dark on load. A lightweight inline script prior to the main bundle execution should read `localStorage` and set `document.documentElement.dataset.theme` early.\n- **Restricted Storage Access**: `localStorage` calls can throw `SecurityError` exceptions in incognito/private windows or restricted enterprise browser policies. All reads and writes must be wrapped in `try...catch` safety guards with a fallback to memory state.\n- **System Scheme Detection**: If fallback to OS preference is implemented, query `window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)')` safely without crashing in environments where `matchMedia` is undefined.\n\n## Engineering Questions\n1. **CSS Delivery**: Should we introduce a global CSS stylesheet with CSS variables, or should we incorporate a styling utility into `package.json`?\n2. **FOUC Prevention**: Can we inject a small inline script into the root HTML template to set the theme attribute prior to React hydration?\n3. **Icon Strategy**: Should we bundle an icon package into `package.json` or maintain standalone SVG components for the toggle in `src/components/Header.jsx`?\n\n## Estimate\n- **Estimate**: 2-3 days (up to 7 days worst case if complete CSS token refactoring is required across all existing views)."}